  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AI, Data and Digital Transformation - Policies, Capacities and Cooperation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governments are under pressure to use AI, data and digital technologies to improve public services, strengthen transparency and respond to citizens&#x2019; needs. At the same time, public institutions face uneven capacities, limited data availability and governance arrangements, human resource gaps and risks related to bias, privacy, exclusion, procurement and accountability. 
UNESCO can support Member States by combining comprehensive assessment of digital environment and formulation of evidence-driven policy-recommendations, competency frameworks, scalable online learning, in-person training, data governance and green AI development support and partnerships with schools of public administration so that digital transformation is inclusive, rights-based and institutionally sustainable.</narrative>
  </description>
